Experiment 3.1: Implement Queue using Stacks (Leetcode Problem-232)
Aim: To implement a Queue using two Stacks and perform FIFO operations such as push, pop, peek, and empty.

Algorithm:
1. Initialize two stacks s1 and s2.
2. Push(x):
     Move all elements from s1 to s2.
     Push x into s1.
     Move all elements back from s2 to s1.
     This keeps the first inserted element on top of s1.
3. Pop():
     Remove and return the top element of s1.
4.Peek():
     Return the top element of s1 without removing it.
5.Empty():
     Check whether s1 is empty.
6.Thus, s1 maintains the FIFO order of the queue.

Code:
class MyQueue {
public:
    stack<int> s1, s2;

    MyQueue() {
        
    }
    
    void push(int x) {
        while (!s1.empty()) {
            s2.push(s1.top());
            s1.pop();
        }

        s1.push(x);

        while (!s2.empty()) {
            s1.push(s2.top());
            s2.pop();
        }
    }
    
